    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.animate\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIn search mode, when navigating to the next occurrence of a search term, the text that shows which occurrence out of all occurrences disappears in some cases.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nv0.10.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Search for text within a file\r\n2. The search term should appear multiple times within the file\r\n3. The search term has a varying number of lines between the next occurrence\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe text that shows the number of occurrences of the search term should always be present.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/30fe399b-7f1d-46ed-a6df-b223791c764c\r\n\r\n",
