            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI am afraid that \"The text that shows the number of occurrences of the search term...\" comes from the other plugin which does not work well with scroll animation. Unfortunately, the only reliable way to perform scroll animation involves actually changing the state of the Neovim (i.e. imitate *actual* scrolling while automatically tracking states between which to scroll) which can affect some other functionality. There are more information [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e50cf9de614500a20e47cfc50e30a100042f91c3/doc/mini-animate.txt#L279-L295).\r\n\r\nClosing as not both not an issue with 'mini.animate' (but some other plugin) and nothing much 'mini.animate' can do here.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nIf you find out which, I can take a look at it. Unless it comes from 'folke/noice.nvim' (which I'd guess it is), in which case I can't help here (because it has a fairly complex code base; also Folke used scroll animation and would have probably fixed it at this point).",
